+- `bin/cedia -p "<prompt>" [-m <model>] [--output-format text|json|stream-json] [--permission read-only|workspace] [--allow <rule>] [--deny <rule>]`: headless run. Read-only unless `--permission workspace`. `--check <cmd>` declares a check for the done gate. `--sandbox auto|on|off` controls the OS sandbox for bash (Linux needs bubblewrap, socat, ripgrep). `--fallback <ref|none>` names the model a run continues on when its quota runs out (default `deepseek` → `anthropic/claude-haiku-5-5`). `--on-quota fallback|wait:<minutes>` waits out a quota that says when it resets, up to that many minutes per run. `--plan <ref>` and `--review <ref>` add the plan and review roles (`claude-code[:<model>]` runs them in the user's own Claude Code); `roles` in `~/.cedia/settings.json` sets all three. `CEDIA_CLAUDE_BIN` points tests at a fake `claude`. Every run is a thread of the project: `--thread <id>` goes on with one, `--handoff-at <n|off>` sets when a long session hands off to a new one, `--spawn on|off` and `--swarm <ref>` control sub-threads.
